  "source_review": {
    "ABI_and_metadata": [
      "128 little-endian U32 descriptor has nonoverlapping fields, reserved63..127 and exact observed size. Raw narrow fields are checked before casts. Model tags and genuine aux header bind the frozen package.",
      "Pointer-free persistent State and decoded Descriptor retain no external AXI pointer. Nine external pointers remain direct top ports; local expected-tag pointer table only refers to constant internal tag arrays.",
      "Shape, frozen WeightKey, op/stage/layer, session identity, sequence, refs, spans and next-epoch checks precede task claims. Maximum task=0xfffffffe: impossible +2 near limit rejects before wrap can match an admitted nonzero task.",
      "LOAD consumes task/W epoch even on started failure. Quant failure consumes only A8 epoch and quant task. Linear claims PS/destination only after complete quant success. Unstarted rejection does not consume claims.",
      "Output state becomes READY only on successful C completion; failure invalidates claimed PS/destination and does not promise rollback of already-written payload."
    ],
    "numeric": [
      "32 signed S8 multiplies are widened to INT32 and reduced with adjacent integer tree; worst absolute magnitude <=524288 fits INT32.",
      "Half converters preserve subnormals and match production RNE behavior. Quant preserves row/group finite-first order, d_full division, reciprocal from unrounded d, half-save check, then per-input F32 product and roundf-away-from-zero.",
      "8-lane finite/replay blocks select the minimum bad input index within each block and stop at the first failed block. Compound i2/i7 NaNs explicitly test first index selection.",
      "Linear performs F32(sa*sw), F32(float(dot)*product), F32(old+term) with +0 old at g0 and bias after all groups. Build uses -fno-fast-math -ffp-contract=off. No FMA or cross-group reassociation appears in source.",
      "Minimum first_rank preserves production tile,row,lane,group,phase order despite m0/group/tile scheduling; per-bank/per-tile masks only suppress later work for that output. Generic multi-tile numerical failure still requires a future runtime regression."
    ],
    "banks_and_tails": [
      "W q mapping: u=b/4,pair=b%4,tile=2*(u/G)+shard,addr=tile*G+u%G; two words enter banks2pair and2pair+1. Scale linear addr4*b+j preserves G82 tile boundaries.",
      "W address cap20991 follows frozen legal T*G<=20992. FP bank addr r*512+k/8 <=8191; A bank r%4 and addr(r/4)*128+g<=511; PS/bias tile<=655.",
      "Rows and N tails are rejected before dot/PS/output. Ordinary output uses local r*N+n; QKV uses production shard/head/plane/global-row formula but has not run in this ACT packet.",
      "Frozen lane_bad[32][656] clearing and compute/bias references are consistent with PS bank/tile. Preliminary P1 alias defect is corrected in reviewed source.",
      "Partition/bind_storage/unroll/pipeline are requests only. lane_bad adds a32x656 control-bit map, beyond the main cache logical totals; actual primitive and timing costs await synthesis."
    ]
  },
  "test_review": {
    "positive": "All final ACT outputs for both batch rows, all256 q bytes and8 half scales per run, selected n0 for batch0/n1 for batch1 eight-group dot/sa/sw/product/term/PS plus bias/final, named trace tails, output neighbors and unused out1, same-W reuse and trace-off equal output. Traces are read from actual arithmetic events.",
    "faults": "Wrong high source-ID, wrong model tag, task replay; compound quant NaNs i2/i7 with quant-only retirement and legal next-epoch recovery; separate-process compound LOAD scale n0/g1 and n1/g0 plus bias NaN with scale n0/g1 winning despite later physical byte offset, followed by exact LOAD/RUN recovery.",
    "oracle_independence": "TB loads frozen independent R0 products. Descriptor generator copies frozen selected trace fields into little-endian bytes without evaluating DUT math. Earlier accepted fixture SHA and all small products remain fixed.",
    "limitations": [
      "Only selected column per batch has full group trace; both final columns are checked for each batch, but all group intermediates for both columns of both batches are not claimed.",
      "TB does not assert observed unused suffix18688..32767; source review finds no write there.",
      "TB does not cover every status detail/high-half/unused-port counter or all composite ABI priorities.",
      "Rows3/5/15/16, QKV, K2624/K4096/N5248, linear error rank and partial writes, zero/subnormal numeric fixtures and epoch boundary tests remain future matrix acceptance work."
    ]
  },
  "compiler_warning_assessment": {
    "warning": "GCC -Waggressive-loop-optimizations in vendor ap_private.h lines6514/6766, inlined from dot32 byte slices and packed A8 writes.",
    "bounded_source_indices": "dot k=0..31 and quant i=8*block+lane with block0..3/lane0..7, so l=8*k or8*i in0..248 and h=l+7 in7..255. h>=l always, no source range overflow.",
    "vendor_branch": "Warnings point to reverse-index branch guarded by l_index>h_index / h_index<l_index. That branch is unreachable for these reviewed call sites.",
    "disposition": "Retain raw warnings; no reachable invalid slice identified by static review, therefore not an ACT CPU acceptance blocker. This is not a general vendor-library UB proof or sanitizer result."
  },
